ead":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.021044623299503185,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":48.4,"_gate_rev_durability":0.21099250205489484,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.030618044554235526,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":45.1,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.004380996983439078,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":55.5,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.01450747953711544,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":75.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.027,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":18.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Western Alliance Bancorporation operates as the bank holding company for Western Alliance Bank that provides various banking products and related services primarily in Arizona, California, and Nevada. It operates through Commercial and Consumer Related segments. The company offers deposit products, including demand deposit, checking, savings, and money market accounts, as well as fixed-rate and fixed maturity certificates of deposit accounts; treasury management products and services to small and middle-market businesses, specialized banking services to sophisticated commercial institutions and investors; and residential mortgage products and services. It also provides commercial and industrial loan products, such as working capital lines of credit, loans to technology companies, inventory and accounts receivable lines, mortgage warehouse lines, equipment loans and leases, and other commercial loans; commercial real estate loans, which are secured by multifamily residential properties, professional offices, industrial facilities, retail centers, hotels, and other commercial properties; construction and land development loans for single family and multifamily residential projects, industrial/warehouse properties, office buildings, retail centers, medical office facilities, and residential lot developments; and consumer loans. In addition, the company offers other financial services, such as internet banking, wire transfers, electronic bill payment and presentment, funds transfer and other digital payment offerings, lock box services, courier, and cash management services. Further, the company holds certain investment securities, municipal and non-profit loans, and leases; invests primarily in low-income housing tax credits and small business investment corporations; and certain real estate loans and related securities. Western Alliance Bancorporation was founded in 1994 and is headquartered in Phoenix, Arizona.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kenneth A. Vecchione | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 71 | Compensation: $5.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $940K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 20%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $14K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Western Alliance Bancorporation is a mid-cap financial services business with a $8.1B market cap on $3.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years and +21% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $2.8B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 4.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.7% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Western Alliance Bancorporation (NYSE:WAL) Price Target Raised to $95.00","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/western-alliance-bancorporation-nysewal-price-target-raised-to-95-00.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793947007.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"How Western Alliance Bancorporation (de) (WAL) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/81/How_Western_Alliance_Bancorporation_de_WAL_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_110426080801_1793797681.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793797681.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Western Alliance Bancorporation (WAL) \u2013 Research Analysts\u2019 Recent Ratings Changes","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/02/western-alliance-bancorporation-wal-research-analysts-recent-ratings-changes.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793633208.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Western Alliance Bancorporation (WAL), Why Is It Drawing Fresh Attention Now?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nyse-wal/western-alliance-bancorporation/news/western-alliance-bancorporation-wal-why-is-it-drawing-fresh","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793594410.123,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.774,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Western Alliance Bancorporation (WAL) Stock May Be Undervalalued After Phoenix Deposit Lead","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nyse-wal/western-alliance-bancorporation/news/western-alliance-bancorporation-wal-stock-may-be-undervalalu","date":"2026-10-31","ti